## System Overview

**Cartoon Search and Rating System:** users search for cartoons, rate them, save them to favourites and manage their accounts. The API handles input validation, user authentication and interactions with the database.

![Cartoon Search and Rating System architecture diagram showing frontend, backend and database components](images/system-architecture.png)

| Layer | Component | Responsibility |
|-------|-----------|----------------|
| Frontend | User Browser | The interface where users interact with the platform |
| Frontend | Home Page | Displays cartoon search, rating and related features |
| Frontend | Login Module | Handles user login and account management |
| Backend | API Gateway | Entry point for all client requests |
| Backend | Authentication Service | Authenticates user credentials and returns auth status |
| Backend | Search Service | Processes cartoon search queries |
| Backend | Rating Service | Manages cartoon ratings |
| Backend | Favorite Service | Manages users' favourite cartoons |
| Backend | User Service | Manages user account details |
| Database | MySQL Database | Stores cartoon data, user information, ratings and favourites |

## Definition of Ready (DoR)

A story is ready to start when we have:

- [ ] Low-fi prototype
- [ ] High-fi prototype
- [ ] Basic framework and workspace
- [ ] Time management for coding
- [ ] List of what's going to give (if we fall behind schedule)
- [ ] Basic planned features
- [ ] Testing requirements

## Definition of Done (DoD)

The release is done when:

- [ ] Basic features are functional
- [ ] Mostly bug-free
- [ ] User testing went well (users satisfied with their experience)
- [ ] Visual design has been finalised
- [ ] Documentation is finished
- [ ] Product owner has approved the project

See [TESTING.md](TESTING.md) for how each testing level links to the DoD.
